# E2E in the same session

When you **finish a feature** or **change user-visible behavior** in this repo, the task is **not done** until `../ecommerce_e2e` has matching Playwright coverage **added or updated in this same chat session**.

## Applies to

- New pages, flows, or interactive UI (auth, cart, checkout, profile, etc.)
- Changes to labels, routes, validation messages, or client/API integration
- Refactors that rename or split controls—pair with `playwright-accessibility` hooks and update specs

## Skip only when

- No observable behavior change (styling-only with same accessibility tree, internal hooks)
- The user explicitly scoped the task without e2e

Say in one line why e2e was skipped.

## Workflow

1. Ship the UI change with stable locators (`playwright-accessibility` rule).
2. Add or update a scenario under `../ecommerce_e2e/tests/` (folder README, one `test()`, mobile storefront viewport per e2e rules).
3. Run that folder’s tests when feasible; fix bugs in the **owning** repo—no test-only workarounds.
4. Mark the feature complete only after e2e is in place or legitimately skipped.

## Maintenance

Any change that alters what users or tests expect requires updating the affected spec in the same session—do not leave scenarios stale or failing.
